  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ae309fc9b93c4434b888290b1d747f9a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TeacherInteraction
  playerMovement: {fileID: 612503862}
  teacherName: Virak
  dialoguePopUp: {fileID: 208243415}
  dialogueManager: {fileID: 1165950374}
  spellSelectionScreen: {fileID: 342678059}
  element: earth
  totalNumOfElementSpells: 3
  battleCanvas: {fileID: 1204102515}
  eventSystem: {fileID: 0}
  initalLines:
  - "What\u2019s up?"
  - "Other than me, I know I\u2019m pretty tall."
  - "Earth magic is such a broad term for so many different magic focuses, and I
    think that \u2018rocks\u2019."
  - From crystals to rocks and metals to sand, control over our surroundings is a
    lot to juggle.
  - Once you get to my level you can even create golems like the one over there.
  - "How about you test your \u2018metal\u2019 against my bot?"
  afterPuzzleLines:
  - Done already?
  - Then we should begin a proper time trial.
  afterBattleLines:
  - Zero errors. Well done.
  - Take this rubber ducky in case you run into larger errors in the future.
  afterSpellLines:
  - Remember, all complex problems can be broken down, just as all complex structures
    stem from simple components like rocks, sands, or metals.
